# Template skin — appearance half (blank; exercises the per-part fallback)
#
# Copy this directory to SYS:Classes/ReIncarnation/Mods/<Name>/, add image
# files beside it, and uncomment the PART lines you supply art for. Every
# part WITHOUT art renders through the procedural Classic path, so a
# partial skin is legal (design E0-2).
#
# Rules (gui/skin.h, fail-closed: one malformed line rejects the file):
# - '#' starts a comment line; unknown keys are ignored.
# - sec = section id 0..17 (gui/ctlreg.h RI_SEC_*; 1 shares 0's art).
# - kind = control kind 0..8 (RI_CK_KNOB..RI_CK_METER).
# - part = [A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,48}. Size-varying parts take a WxH suffix in
#   2x-master pixels, e.g. knob.frame.40x56 (design E0-9).
# - file = image path relative to this directory, PNG/RGBA recommended
#   (per-pixel alpha survives picture.class; ILBM cannot carry alpha).
# - NFRAMES = frames in a vertical strip, 1..256 (64 = classic look).
#
# Key inventory (uncomment + point at files as supplied):
#
# Section backdrops (one per section; 2x-master px == Q units numerically):
# BACKGROUND.0=bg00.png
# BACKGROUND.2=bg02.png
# BACKGROUND.3=bg03.png
# BACKGROUND.4=bg04.png
# BACKGROUND.5=bg05.png
# BACKGROUND.6=bg06.png
# BACKGROUND.7=bg07.png
# BACKGROUND.8=bg08.png
# BACKGROUND.9=bg09.png
# BACKGROUND.10=bg10.png
# BACKGROUND.11=bg11.png
# BACKGROUND.12=bg12.png
# BACKGROUND.13=bg13.png
# BACKGROUND.14=bg14.png
# BACKGROUND.15=bg15.png
# BACKGROUND.16=bg16.png
# BACKGROUND.17=bg17.png
#
# Knob frame strips (one per section + knob size; value->frame is
# value*frames/128, see ri_skin_frame):
# PART.0.0.knob.frame.84x120=knob_84x120.png,64
# PART.2.0.knob.frame.40x56=knob_40x56.png,64
# PART.2.0.knob.frame.36x44=knob_36x44.png,64
# PART.3.0.knob.frame.44x52=knob_44x52.png,64
# PART.4.0.knob.frame.45x70=knob_45x70.png,64
# PART.10.0.knob.frame.48x80=knob_48x80.png,64
# PART.13.0.knob.frame.50x90=knob_50x90.png,64
#
# Future parts (no call sites yet — lookup helper exists):
# PART.<sec>.<kind>.fader.cap=<file>,1
# PART.<sec>.5.step.lit=<file>,1
# PART.<sec>.7.digit.strip=<file>,10
